# ============================ VinaX environment ============================
# Frontend (Vite). PUBLIC — never put secrets in VITE_* variables.
# Optional overrides; the app works with none of these set.
# VITE_API_BASES=https://saavn.dev/api,https://saavn.sumit.co/api
# VITE_APP_NAME=VinaX

# ------- Server-side secrets (Cloudflare WORKER `vinax-api`) -------
# Set with: npx wrangler secret put <NAME> --config worker/wrangler.toml
# (or Workers dashboard -> vinax-api -> Settings -> Variables & Secrets).
# They live on the Worker, never on Pages, and never reach the client.
# This file documents names only — real values belong in Cloudflare (or a local
# .dev.vars for `npm run dev:worker`, which is gitignored).
#
# AI lanes — generation-4 env names (each lane pins its own model + provider
# base in code — see functions/_lib/ai.ts LANE_BASE; NVIDIA NIM keys are
# nvapi-... unless noted):
#   VINAX_DEEPSEEK_V4_FLASH   PRIMARY — chat · AI Playlists · assistant (VinaX FLASH)
#   VINAX_CHATGPT_20_B        fast chat · quick tasks · instant answers (VinaX 20B)
#   VINAX_NEMOTRON_SUPER      deep thinking · the Think button (VinaX SUPER)
#   VINAX_GROQ_API_KEY        music knowledge · lyrics tools · Q&A (VinaX INSTANT)
#                             GROQ console key (gsk_...) — this lane calls api.groq.com
#   VINAX_CHATGPT_120_B       AI DJ · Aura Mix · Smart Radio · smart queue (VinaX 120B)
#   VINAX_NEMOTRON_ULTRA      Home Screen Builder · trending · LIVE VOICE (VinaX ULTRA)
#   VINAX_NVIDIA_NEMOTRON_3_NANO_30B_A3B
#                             Search-page music expert · personalized song
#                             discovery (VinaX NANO 3) — also signs the lane's
#                             secondary model (NVIDIA keys are account-scoped)
#   NVIDIA_BASE_URL           optional DEFAULT endpoint override (lanes without a LANE_BASE pin)
#
# Database: Cloudflare D1 — no secrets needed. The Worker's DB binding in
# wrangler.toml is the whole configuration; the schema auto-creates on first
# use (worker/functions/_lib/db.ts). R2 nightly backups use the BACKUPS
# binding; global rate limiting uses the RATE_LIMIT Durable Object — all
# declared in wrangler.toml, none of them secret.
#
# Admin console (…/admin — gates every /api/admin endpoint):
#   ADMIN_LOGIN_PASSWORD   long random secret
#
# Web push (VAPID keypair, generate once and keep):
#   VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY       base64url, 65-byte uncompressed P-256 point
#   VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY      base64url, 32-byte P-256 scalar
#   VAPID_SUBJECT          mailto:owner@example.com
#
# Telemetry / device-id signing (audit finding H-SRV-6):
#   TELEMETRY_PEPPER       HMAC pepper for aggregate-mode device-id hashing;
#                          also seeds the in-memory rate-limiter key hash so
#                          plaintext IPs never sit in isolate memory
#                          (H-SRV-11). Set a long random secret.
#   DEVICE_ID_SECRET       HMAC secret for /api/events signed_device_id.
#                          The client stores signed_device_id_next returned
#                          from first-contact posts and echoes it forever
#                          after. Falls back to TELEMETRY_PEPPER when unset,
#                          but a dedicated value is recommended so the two
#                          can be rotated independently.
#
# Scheduled jobs (GitHub Actions cron -> /api/cron/*):
#   CRON_SECRET            shared secret; requests without it are rejected
#                          (header x-cron-secret only — ?key= is no longer
#                          accepted, audit finding H-SRV-7)
#
# Optional integrations:
#   BRAVE_API_KEY          web search inside VinaX AI
#   GITHUB_REPO            owner/repo used by the APK release endpoint
#   GITHUB_TOKEN           optional; raises GitHub API rate limits

# Native Android background push (FCM) — optional; enables notifications
# even when the app is fully closed. See docs/fcm-push-setup.md.
#   FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT   Firebase service-account JSON (whole file, as a string)
